// A module is referenced by its path's last segment, so two files of the same name in different
// directories both want to be `patient`. That used to be accepted silently with the first `use` winning:
// every `patient.x` went to model's, and the second line did nothing -- a wrong function quietly called.
// It is an error now, which is the rule the per-name `use` form always had. Reported rather than resolved
// by inventing a name from two path segments, because a name the author never wrote is what this module
// system sets out to avoid, and `as` already says it explicitly.
use model/patient
use entity/patient

fn main() {
    print(patient.name())
}
